            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Bengali for to look for, then the Bengali for to lose."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: পরা",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "পরা — pôrā — \"to wear\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "পরা (pôrā) is a tadbhava, a word inherited from Sanskrit and reshaped by sound change. It comes from paridadhāti, \"sets round, puts on clothes\" (CDIAL 7835). CDIAL notes that Chatterji preferred the passive paridhīyate."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
